formatp <- function(p_value){
  formatted_p <- ifelse(p_value<0.001,'<.001',as.character(format(round(p_value,3),nsmall=3)))
  return(formatted_p)
}
formatnum <- function(integer){
    if(is.numeric(integer)){
        text=c('zero','one','two','three','four','five','six','seven','eight','nine','ten')
        formatted_num <- ifelse(integer > 10 | integer < 0, integer, text[integer+1])
        return(formatted_num)
    }else{"ENTER AN INTEGER"}
}
@

<<exclusions, echo=FALSE>>=
# handle exclusions
S1_all=S1_preExclusion |> filter(completed==1, attentionPassed==1, time_exclusion==0, time_straightliner_exclusion==0) |>
mutate(age_1=as.numeric(age_1),political_leaning=as.numeric(political_leaning))

@

After providing informed consent (ERB # ANONYMIZED), participants completed an online survey consisting of two main parts: In Part 1, participants were asked to recall details about one specific DKO. Participants were randomly assigned to one of the three focal topics (health, politics, or the environment). Those who were unable to recall a DKO about the assigned topic were first asked to recall a DKO about another focal topic. Participants who did not recall any societally-relevant DKO, were asked to recall a DKO about any topic. In Part 2, participants were asked to report experiences with and impressions of societally-relevant DKOs in general. The pre-registration, measures, and analysis scripts are available on our OSF page. 

\subsection{Participants}

We recruited Dutch-speaking participants via the panel company Dynata, based on quotas representing the Dutch population in terms of age, gender, and education (see details in supplementary materials). $\Sexpr{sum(S1_preExclusion$completed==1)}$ completed the survey. In accordance with our pre-registration, we excluded participants who failed two out of three attention checks (N=$\Sexpr{sum(S1_preExclusion$completed==1 & S1_preExclusion$attentionPassed==0)}$), those who completed the survey implausibly fast (N=$\Sexpr{sum(S1_preExclusion$completed==1 & S1_preExclusion$attentionPassed==1 & S1_preExclusion$time_exclusion==1)}$) or unusually fast with a high percentage of straightlined answers (see analysis scrips for details; N=$\Sexpr{sum(S1_preExclusion$completed==1 & S1_preExclusion$attentionPassed==1 & S1_preExclusion$time_straightliner_exclusion==1)}$). A final sample of $\Sexpr{sum(S1_preExclusion$completed==1 & S1_preExclusion$attentionPassed==1 & S1_preExclusion$time_exclusion==0 & S1_preExclusion$time_straightliner_exclusion==0)}$ participants (Mage=$\Sexpr{round(mean(S1_all$age_1),2)}$, SDage=$\Sexpr{round(sd(S1_all$age_1),2)}$) were included in the analysis. $\Sexpr{sum(S1_all$gender==1)}$ participants reported their gender identity as female, $\Sexpr{sum(S1_all$gender==2)}$ as male, $\Sexpr{sum(S1_all$gender==3)}$ as non-binary, and $\Sexpr{sum(S1_all$gender==4)}$ as other. The sample is educationally (N=$\Sexpr{sum(S1_all$Education==1)}$ no formal education or elementary school, N=$\Sexpr{sum(S1_all$Education==2)}$ Vmbo, havo/vwo-onderbouw, mbo1, N=$\Sexpr{sum(S1_all$Education==3)}$ Havo, VWO, mbo2-4, N=$\Sexpr{sum(S1_all$Education==4)}$ Hbo/vwo-bachelor, N=$\Sexpr{sum(S1_all$Education==5)}$ Hbo/vwo-master or doctorate) and politically diverse (M=$\Sexpr{round(mean(S1_all$political_leaning,na.rm=T),2)}$, SD=$\Sexpr{round(sd(S1_all$political_leaning,na.rm=T),2)}$ on a scale from 0=politically left to 10=politically right).

Of these participants, we excluded an additional $\Sexpr{sum(S1_all$conv_topic_FLAG==1,na.rm=T)}$ datapoints from analyses of specific recalled societally-relevant DKOs for not naming an interpretable specific topic within the target category and $\Sexpr{sum(S1_all$conv_topic==4,na.rm=T)}$ observations for recalling a DKO about a non-focal topic.

